WEBVTT

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:26.250
Your can't-miss target is a sniper that is at the very top of his class.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.380
He's the reason why we picked you, Spartacus.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.380
You can sing your praises after my work is done.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:40.850
I'm the head of a South African gold mining enterprise, Rosmacdonald.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.270
This is the president of a Swedish computer firm, Pettensen.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:52.530
The truth is we need you to take care of
a man who is trying to end both of our lives.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.780
This man.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.540
We'll pay you $500,000 in advance if you accept.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:05.790
$500,000 is too cheap a price to take care of that man.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.540
I'll need $500,000 more.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.550
A-A million dollars? That is not what you told me.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:17.550
Marco, didn't your research say his price per hit ranges from $200,000 to $500,000?

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:18.800
Uh... yes.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:21.350
If we can't compromise, then that's that.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.810
Call me if there's another.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.640
Wait, Spartacus!

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.940
For anyone else, this job would be impossible!

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:32.820
I can't think of anyone other than you who can take on Golgo 13.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.700
Mr. Rosmacdonald! Mr. Pettensen!

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.530
Fine, fine, we'll pay the $1 million.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.740
Right, Pettensen?

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:43.200
Sure.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.920
I walk unsteadily on paths to nowhere

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.050
wondering what I should do right now.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:04.520
I play the song you like on the car stereo

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.060
with the volume up and my feelings crystallized

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.690
driving on streets with no crossroads or signals

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.110
with a speed that will catch up with you.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.580
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:30.880
And let's not bother with the breaks - full throttle.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.170
Oh someday - one of these days

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:40.260
You'll be at my place where nobody can find you.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:46.350
Whenever you suffer a breakdown one can't see

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.940
depend on me for your repairs.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:56.320
So faraway - let's run!

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:02.530
We'll reset and start again - even at our limit.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:06.830
Oh someday - one of these days

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.880
If I'm with you we'll find our dream.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:28.220
The Brutes' Banquet

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:33.480
Our high-sensitivity vision cameras and
infrared cameras altogether make eight.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.520
How's your end?

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:38.230
Yes, remote control functions are all online.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.650
And the mikes are perfectly good to go?

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:45.410
Yes. We've installed the high-fidelity mikes and boom mikes everywhere.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.660
Not even an ant can crawl without us hearing it.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.290
All right, let's move out.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.760
This is Marco, everything's in place.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.550
All the hidden cameras and microphones are working flawlessly.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:15.190
We won't be having any police or curious onlookers on our hands, will we Marco?

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:18.650
Don't worry, not even a stray kitten can get in there.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:23.570
We went through all the channels to make sure the Colosseum is completely reserved.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:24.360
Hmm?

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:32.250
Can you turn on the switch so we can test the TV transmission?

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:32.250
Sure.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.670
We can see it clearly. Looks great.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.760
Okay, you have two hours until the main event. Enjoy.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.720
Mm-hmm, good work.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.770
We can now watch the century's greatest duel live.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.770
Just the two of us.

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:57.520
We are running out of brutish ways to entertain ourselves.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.570
<i>Kill them!</i>

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.580
Compared to this, all the others will be mere child's play.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.120
Just two more hours, huh? I can hardly wait.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:27.820
Hey!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.490
Spartacus just saw something!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.330
Get Camera Five on his field of vision.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:33.740
Yes sir!

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.330
H-He's here!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.780
You've finally made it, Golgo 13.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.450
He's here! Golgo 13's here!

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.870
Mm-hmm. It finally begins.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:19.460
Yeah.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.920
You were very quick to accept my challenge.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:32.720
I guess you were stung when I told you over the phone that you'll be considered 2nd-rate if you declined?

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.050
No.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:39.810
I only wanted to see what makes a pro like you behave like this.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.820
I'm ready when you are.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.450
Listen up.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.660
Don't you miss a second of this duel. These things only last a moment you know.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.120
Uh, yes.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.500
Wh-What this? Why aren't they moving? Why aren't they shooting?

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.550
No, it's not that they won't move, they <i>can't</i>  move!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.130
Th-This is it! The real McCoy!

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:17.180
Well, this is certainly a million-dollar show.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.200
Fire!

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:46.540
How did it go? What happened?

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.170
Who got who?

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.340
Close up! We need a close up!

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.720
Get their faces, now!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.090
O-Of course!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:05.770
Huh?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:30.460
Y... You probably want to finish me off.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.300
Your gun must have... at least...

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.130
I'm out of bullets.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:38.470
I planned on saving one last round.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:40.430
But your maneuvering was superb.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.680
Same goes for you.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:47.270
But I got hit in the stomach... I'm done for.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:55.190
Well, I should be happy that I at least kept Golgo 13 from delivering the finishing shot because he spent all his bullets.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.950
Why did you agree to be a part of this show?

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.820
Show?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:04.700
They've put up dozens of TV cameras and microphones around us.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:08.710
Someone somewhere is watching this.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.710
What did you say?

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.880
M... Mr. Marco?

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.590
You're right. I can see it now.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:23.510
So they didn't hire me to protect them.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:28.850
They just wanted to see a deathmatch between us.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.610
How stupid of me.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:36.610
I put my life on the line just so they can play around with me.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:43.950
They're despicable... simply abominable. They will pay.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.790
E... Even if I'm dead and in the ground.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:53.380
Gabriel Rosmacdonald and Ingemar Pettensen.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.630
You must put an end to those two, Golgo 13.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:05.890
I know better than anyone that a pro like you isn't
going to do anything out of sympathy or compassion.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.640
In fact, I don't even want you to.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.900
I have no relatives.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:19.150
I will leave with over $3 million in a Swiss bank account that will remain unclaimed.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.660
I want to use that to hire you.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:28.540
My secret account number...

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.920
...is written in the lining of my left breast pocket.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:36.920
So... do we have a deal, Golgo 13?

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:44.300
Please give me an answer... before it's too late.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.430
Okay, I accept.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:19.170
Golgo 13 just accepted a job from Spartacus!

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:23.800
S-So Golgo 13 is really going to come kill us?

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:26.470
H-How did this happen?!

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:30.180
Marco! Did you hear what they just said to each other?

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:32.730
I've already called some people.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.310
Please remain calm. I've just got off the phone with the Sicilian Mafia.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:41.320
Giuseppe Mangarno has just gathered 20 of his best men.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:45.320
They are now coming over to provide a security detail.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.120
Give me that!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:53.790
We're talking about Golgo 13 here! Will that be even enough?!

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.330
It's all right.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:13:00.050
When they heard that they were facing Golgo 13, a bunch of pros jumped at the chance to prove themselves.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:04.300
You two must remain where you are and not go anywhere.

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.970
All right, agreed.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:19.690
Aha! Let's go to my mansion in Johannesburg.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:27.240
We have top-of-the-line security at my South African mines that can ward off any insurrection or invasion.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.240
We even have 300 soldiers at our beck and call.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.290
So why don't we take flight to Africa?

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.500
Hmm...

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:38.500
I don't feel safe with just a Mafia security detail.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.840
And there's no way we can get your kind of security here.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.300
Good! Then it's settled!

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:44.090
Huh?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.090
Hmm?

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:46.260
Who's there?

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.470
A Mr. Mangarno is here to see you.

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:59.270
We've received orders from our base in Sicily to guard you two.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.810
We've been waiting!

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:05.860
We've just finished our discussion, which means you gentlemen won't be working here.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:11.870
You'll be taking us, now while we're still alive, to Johannesburg where Golgo 13 can't reach us.

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.750
Johannesburg, you say?

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:15.750
That's right.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.870
We don't care how much it costs. Just make sure we're safe!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.810
Do you know how many times I've been body checked?!

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:42.150
And now I find out that my ticket has been canceled?

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:46.650
We've received a bomb threat from terrorists, then someone committed arson to our building.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:50.740
Except for military planes and one international flight, the entire airport is on lockdown.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.990
That flight only goes out once a week!

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:57.000
And did you actually change the aircraft?!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:02.750
You switched a jumbo jet with a smaller Boeing 727. You're just trying to limit the number of passengers!

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:19.730
Everything's going according to plan.

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:24.480
We've set off a bomb at one of their buildings and sent a terror threat.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:29.740
And just as we anticipated, they've deployed the army, which will keep you two safe.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.660
Why can't we use a private jet?

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.740
I have one in Switzerland.

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:39.830
Golgo 13 is a man who can easily shoot down private planes.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:46.670
However, even he isn't going to be heedless with a fully-booked, regular, economy-class passenger flight.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.010
Why did you switch the plane with a small-sized Boeing?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.010
You'll soon see for yourself.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:17.870
What's with these lights?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.660
They're a cover.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:23.330
They can maintain nearly the same overwhelming brightness for 1.5 kilometers.

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:26.250
Although that's well within Golgo's range

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:31.880
he cannot shoot from that distance even if he uses infrared or night-vision.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:35.890
The light from our cars can even short out a Starlight scope.

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.480
The plane's all clear!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.650
All the economy-class passengers have been checked.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.900
We changed the plane because of this ramp.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:55.410
Rather than putting you two through too much exposure, we went for a model that allows you to board directly.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.200
I see!

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.780
What's with that plane?

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:00.790
That's the plane the troops used to deploy here.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:04.160
In any event, that's none of our concern.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:25.390
The soldiers from my gold mines are being dispatched to the Johannesburg airport.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:29.480
But what's going to happen now that we're going to refuel at Nairobi, Kenya?

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.320
No need to worry.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:35.150
We've gave an order via an international call and they are fortifying their security as we speak.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:42.490
Plus our men have personally checked everybody getting on passenger planes in Rome heading for Africa.

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:47.750
Anyway, this plane will be the first to arrive in Johannesburg from Italy.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:50.130
You two are free to relax.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:53.880
Okay. You just concentrate on getting us there safely.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:03.680
It will be one hour before we reach Johannesburg.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:10.940
Giuseppe, even if we are taking refuge at the mines, do you think Golgo 13 is still coming after us?

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:14.320
He did sustain an injury during his duel with Spartacus.

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:17.200
We must still remain cautious.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:19.820
That man can't be reckoned with using common sense.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:05.870
We're here.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:09.830
Whew, we've made it in one piece.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:14.380
Once we get to our militarily secured mines, we can truly rest easy.

00:19:14.380 --> 00:19:18.130
Well Giuseppe, it looks like you've earned yourself a bonus.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:21.130
That's very gracious of you.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.120
There's no need for that, Mr. Rosmacdonald.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.870
Golgo 13 couldn't have possibly arrived before us.

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.380
That's right.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:07.600
Hmm?

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:22.820
I-Impossible! That's downright impossible!

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.820
Where the hell did he...?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:28.830
H-Hey!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:29.830
What's that plane?

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:34.210
Th-That's a special military plane that flew non-stop from Rome.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:40.460
It's loaded with foreign troops who are headed for a neighboring country to suppress anti-government forces.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.470
It landed here 30 minutes earlier for refueling.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.470
It came non-stop from Rome?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:51.220
I get it. It passed us while we were refueling in Nairobi.

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:55.230
That son of a bitch. Golgo 13.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:17.250
Oh-ho? So you also joined the international forces just so you can kill people?

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.510
It sure is sweet to kill people <i>and</i>  get paid for it.

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:29.010
I've killed dozens of those primitives during my time in Africa, but I've yet to see one that has some fight in him.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.520
Wait, there was one...

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.560
It was during an internal strife in Congo.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.560
It was this guerrilla leader we engaged.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:42.150
We damn nearly got wiped out.

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.410
That man had some weird-ass name.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:51.330
He took it from a leader of a Roman slave uprising.

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:56.540
Hmm... crap, what was it again?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.880
Spartacus.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:03.260
Yeah, that's right! Spartacus!

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.340
He sure picked a name for himself!

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:08.970
That guy's gonna be a big shot, I tell you!

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:47.050
I  was worried with no one to talk to.

00:22:47.050 --> 00:22:50.090
I was brooding and standing still

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:52.260
without moving a muscle.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:55.430
I wonder when that was?

00:22:55.930 --> 00:22:57.140
I'm sure

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:00.310
you agonized over how

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:05.570
people will hurt themselves and other people

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:08.820
and fail to realize it.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:09.950
When

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:13.370
the same days keep repeating themselves

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:15.620
you never change.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:17.870
Since you're here for me

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:22.170
I will accept the way that I am.

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:26.420
I will never leave you alone

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:29.760
I will softly touch your trembling heart.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:36.640
I realized that I'm not the only one who's alone.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:39.810
We're enveloped in the gentle sun beams.

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:43.150
The long winter is finally over.

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:49.780
The parts of us that were lonely will surely get stronger.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.540
It's the dead of night in London.

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:09.050
A mysterious woman propositions Golgo in the foggy neighborhood of Petticoat Lane.

00:24:09.050 --> 00:24:12.590
Suddenly, they face some men who are coming for the kill.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:16.390
Golgo takes the woman and leaves the neighborhood.

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:19.720
The mystery will be solved at the end of their flight.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:25.690
Night Fog in Petticoat Lane

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:24.730
Next time on Golgo 13: Night Fog in Petticoat Lane.

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:28.150
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
